# gitleaks allowlist.
#
# Every entry below is a synthetic credential in a test fixture. They exist
# because ContentSanitizer's whole job is to redact secrets out of captured
# transcripts, and testing a redactor requires strings shaped like the thing it
# redacts. None has ever been a live credential.
#
# They are listed here so a public clone does not greet a reader with ten
# security findings that all resolve to "this is the test for the redactor".
#
# Fingerprints are commit:file:rule:line and are tied to specific commit SHAs.
# A history rewrite invalidates them -- regenerate with:
#   gitleaks detect --source . --log-opts="--all --full-history" \
#     --report-format json --report-path /tmp/gl.json --redact=0
#   jq -r '.[] | "\(.Commit):\(.File):\(.RuleID):\(.StartLine)"' /tmp/gl.json

